## Licensing Notes (informational)

This is the standard MIT License text. The choice rationale:

- **Why MIT:** course materials benefit from maximum reuse — instructors at other
  institutions can adapt modules, and students can carry their scripts anywhere.
- **Dataset exceptions:** individual datasets under `datasets/` may carry their own
  documented license in their `README.md` (e.g., CC0 or Open Data Commons for
  imported public data). That license governs the data files; the course text
  remains MIT.
- **Third-party trademarks:** Ubuntu®, VirtualBox®, Docker®, and other product
  names belong to their owners. Their use here is descriptive and does not imply
  endorsement.
- **Before official adoption,** an institution may wish to have counsel review the
  license choice and the copyright line (e.g., to name the university instead of
  the contributors).
